  :adr/deploy-shape-6493 "worker/ subdirectory in the same repo (not a split repo); routes.cljc is a pure sync (store,request)->response handler wrapping factoring.operation's existing langgraph-clj StateGraph UNCHANGED; worker.cljs is the async Cloudflare translation (CORS, real store-round-trip /health, Bearer-token auth); kv_store.cljs hydrates/persists the WHOLE book through ONE Cloudflare KV key as a pr-str'd EDN snapshot (hydrate-compute-persist, a deliberate divergence from cloud-murakumo-fleet's per-key streaming op-map, reasoning: this actor's HARD checks aggregate across multiple stored records, re-deriving that logic a second time as async code would risk drift from the JVM-tested version)"
  :adr/store-additions-6493 "factoring.store gained four small additive functions (snapshot/from-snapshot/empty-db/empty-state) and one new protocol method (register-funder!, on both MemStore and DatomicStore) -- the governed core (Store protocol, factoring.governor/factoring.operation/factoring.phase) is otherwise UNCHANGED from ADR-2607141700"
  :adr/public-transparency-surface-6493 "GET /health, /fee-schedule, /solvency/attestation(s), /funders are unauthenticated by design -- gating them would defeat the anti-Zentoshin purpose ADR-2607141700 built. Every other route requires FACTORING_API_KEY (Bearer/X-Api-Key), fails CLOSED (503) if unconfigured -- deliberately unlike cloud-murakumo-fleet's own fail-open precedent, given this actor's actuation-decision routes"
  :adr/human-in-the-loop-over-http-6493 "factoring.operation's interrupt-before models human sign-off as a separate resume call; with no separate approval UI, an authenticated caller's own request to a gated actuation route IS that sign-off (routes.cljc/run-op! auto-resumes an :escalate disposition within the same HTTP call). HARD violations still hold, un-overridably -- only the SOFT confidence/actuation-approval gate is collapsed into one round trip, not the governor itself"
  :adr/live-smoke-test-6493 "full lifecycle curled end-to-end against https://factoring.murakumo.cloud before landing: funder registration, intake, verify, underwrite, a stale-attestation HOLD, a solvency attestation publish, actuation 1 (advance), collect, actuation 2 (settle), a double-advance HOLD -- the resulting audit ledger (GET /ledger) was read back and confirmed to match exactly. Caught and fixed TWO real bugs before landing: (1) empty-POST-body crash (.json() on a bodyless action route, fixed with a defensive text-then-JSON.parse pattern) (2) JSON-string-vs-Clojure-keyword mismatch on :debtor-risk-tier that silently broke the fee-schedule exact-match check forever (JSON has no keyword type; js->clj :keywordize-keys true only keywordizes map KEYS not values; fixed with a boundary coercion at intake). Both regression-tested in worker/test/routes_test.clj. Test data (one funder, two receivables) deleted from live KV afterward (wrangler kv key delete book --remote) -- deployment starts from a genuinely empty book"
  :adr/honesty-boundary-6493 "this deployment makes the GOVERNED DECISION software live, callable and durable at a real HTTPS URL. It does NOT wire any real bank transfer/payment rail, real funder capital, or real KYC/AML provider, and does not claim any real money moves through it. :advance/fund and :reserve/settle remain governed, audited DECISION POINTS -- an authorized caller gets a real, audited, HARD-check-enforced commit/hold disposition and ledger entry, but no real currency moves anywhere, because no real bank/payment integration is attached and none is fabricated. The value delivered is a live, production, governed decision+transparency service a real licensed operator could point real capital and real banking rails at -- governance/audit/transparency machinery is fully live and real; the money-movement backend is intentionally not attached"
  :adr/secrets-bookkeeping-6493 "FACTORING_API_KEY set via wrangler secret put (never committed), mirrored in 1Password gftdcojp vault (item: cloud-itonami-isic-6493 FACTORING_API_KEY (factoring.murakumo.cloud)) for operator recovery"
